ransfer&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.fixed_word_transfer&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&ref=sha256%3A47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.fixed_word_transfer","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"BFMVZ Theorem 1 is a fixed-depth, fixed-angle identity. It does not transfer raw seeded, masked or controlled words, give a joint n,p,D limit, or certify the construction preceding seed removal.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-fixed-word-transfer","bfmvz2022_tree_transfer","fggz2022_fixed_depth"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.fixed_word_transfer","kind":"claim","label":"Fixed ordinary tree word transfers to fixed-angle SK","locator":"02-foundations.tex:3–45; prop:tree-transfer; BFMVZ arXiv:2110.14206v3, §2.1–2.2, equations (2.3),(2.6),(6.1)–(6.3), Theorem 1 and §6 proof","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-foundations","statement":"For every fixed finite ordinary cost/mixer word W, the Gaussian SK thermodynamic limiting expected energy per spin equals lim_{D→∞}(√D/2)⟨Z_iZ_j⟩_W for an edge of the (D+1)-regular tree with cost D^(−1/2)Σ_{ij}Z_iZ_j. The manuscript converts the BFMVZ negative tree-cost convention by conjugating X on one tree bipartition, which flips cost and edge correlation while preserving mixer and plus state.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.fixed_word_transfer","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation%22%2C%22circuit.fixed_wor